\f1\fs26 Rick and Dick were guys who broke into houses and placed covert listening devices and cameras\'97and occasionally, bombs and other hilarious booby traps. They undertook physical surveillance. They did nasty jobs no one else wanted.\
Unfortunately, doing nasty nasty jobs no one else wanted was far from a full-time occupation, so they often moonlighted as ambulance punks.\
Earlier, a body in the street had been reported, so they claimed the job and drove their multi-purpose surveillance van disguised as a coronial pick-up unit around to check it out. Once there, they procrastinated. They still had hours remaining on their shift.\
\'93He\'92s not going anywhere,\'94 the passenger punk said.\
 So they got meat pies and coffee, and sat in the tricked-up ambulance, watching morning commuters avoid the man in the midnight blue suit lying dead in the street. They were hoping for some weak-stomached folks to squeal or\'97please, please!\'97vomit, but everyone swept around the body with a practised, professional duty of neglect.\
That was until some cleaner, with the arse out of his overalls, almost pushed his cart right over the dead man. When the cleaner tripped and fell on the body, Rick and Dick laughed so hard, they sprayed flakes of pie pastry and tomato sauce all over the dashboard.
